          "syncMarkdown": "We appreciate your suggestion to evaluate terminal-only supervision under the same model structure. We retain the same recurrent latent tokens, final visual block, and trainable modules, but train using only terminal visual supervision and the generation loss. This control uses 1,253 planner updates and 537 generator updates. The table compares this new run with the full PhysFlow results reported in the paper.\n\nEditing accuracy (%) on PICABench-Superficial.\n\n| Training strategy | LP | LSE | RFL | RFR | DFM | CSL | GST | LST | Overall |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Terminal-only supervision | 53.84 | 64.48 | 57.73 | 59.18 | 42.57 | 46.68 | 63.59 | 55.71 | 55.57 |\n| Full PhysFlow | 54.45 | 65.19 | 58.52 | 57.99 | 44.91 | 47.31 | 64.32 | 56.43 | 56.32 |\n\nFull PhysFlow improves overall accuracy by 0.75 percentage points over terminal-only supervision. This comparison demonstrates the benefit of our training strategy: textual rationales and intermediate visual states provide process supervision that improves physical editing accuracy beyond terminal supervision alone.",
          "markdown": "We appreciate your suggestion to evaluate terminal-only supervision under the same model structure. We retain the same recurrent latent tokens, final visual block, and trainable modules, but train using only terminal visual supervision and the generation loss. This control uses 1,253 planner updates and 537 generator updates. The table compares this new run with the full PhysFlow results reported in the paper.\n\nEditing accuracy (%) on PICABench-Superficial.\n\n| Training strategy | LP | LSE | RFL | RFR | DFM | CSL | GST | LST | Overall |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Terminal-only supervision | 53.84 | 64.48 | 57.73 | 59.18 | 42.57 | 46.68 | 63.59 | 55.71 | 55.57 |\n| Full PhysFlow | 54.45 | 65.19 | 58.52 | 57.99 | 44.91 | 47.31 | 64.32 | 56.43 | 56.32 |\n\nFull PhysFlow improves overall accuracy by 0.75 percentage points over terminal-only supervision. This comparison demonstrates the benefit of our training strategy: textual rationales and intermediate visual states provide process supervision that improves physical editing accuracy beyond terminal supervision alone.",
